00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:10.960
This is Heinz Lemke at his PDP-7 with a Teletype and
a Type 340 vector graphics display and a light pen

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.880
showing PIXIE that he developed at Cambridge
University that has one of the first known

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:25.520
radial menus operated by a light pen. So you, that
cursor in the center is what you can draw with

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.680
and the menu items are around the cursor. Also,
there's menu items along the right edge of the

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:40.240
screen to set the different modes for drawing.
And if you just touch this with the light pen,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:48.000
that runs the command. And then it tracks by
putting these dots on the screen. Now, see how

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.080
you can move it around by dragging the middle. And
then you can pop up the menu to select different

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:03.680
components and the menu travels along with you.
And the neat thing is you can draw a line and then

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:12.800
undo it by moving back along the line or just do
diagonal lines and attach things. So this is a

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:19.840
general purpose drawing editor and it's a vector
graphics display with beautiful green phosphor.

